      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Or maybe what we should actually do is to update e820, before inserting resources, like we do in `e820__reserve_setup_data()`, for example?\n\nLooks like that is what we should actually do. See e.g. `e820__setup_pci_gap()`: it searches for a gap between e820 regions, to use it for PCI memory. So if our DT reserved region is not reflected in any e820 entry, it may result in PCI memory overlapping with our DT region?\n\n...BTW slightly offtopic: if `e820__setup_pci_gap()` guarantees that PCI memory will not overlap with e820 regions, why is it needed to postpone inserting resources for e820 reserved regions until `e820__reserve_resources_late()`? IIUC because kernel prefers not to reallocate initial BAR values unless necessary, in particular it keeps them even if they overlap with e820 reserved regions (but not if they overlap with e820 RAM regions). https://lore.kernel.org/all/alpine.LFD.1.10.0808281255200.3300@nehalem.linux-foundation.org/",
      "parentUuid": "7c666538_728191a5",
      "revId": "4cec988fea52cc9bdd28f42ca71d825e6e0cf374",
